<%- include('../partials/layout-start') %>
<%- include('../partials/page-header', {
  icon: 'bi-person-x',
  heading: 'Close your account',
  sub: 'What happens, said plainly, before you do it.'
}) %>
<section class="glass-section pb-5"><div class="container">
  <div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-8">
    <%- include('../partials/flash') %>

    <div class="glass-card mb-4"><div class="card-body p-4">
      <h2 class="h6 mb-3">What is destroyed</h2>
      <p class="small text-muted-2">
        Your name, your email address, your password, the country and address your sign-up
        came from, and any answers you gave about gender or date of birth. Your profile goes
        with it: your photo, your CV, your work history, your projects, your certifications
        and your skills. Saved jobs, votes and quiz attempts go too. None of it is recoverable
        and none of it is kept in a backup copy this site can read back.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h6 mb-3 mt-4">What stays, and why</h2>
      <p class="small text-muted-2">
        Some records are not only yours. They stay, with nothing left in them that points at a
        person — your account carries no name or address afterwards, so nothing here can
        identify you.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-unstyled small mb-0">
        <% retained.forEach(function (row) { %>
          <li class="border-top py-2">
            <strong><%= row[0] %></strong>
            <div class="text-muted-2"><%= row[1] %></div>
          </li>
        <% }); %>
      </ul>
    </div></div>

    <div class="glass-card border-danger"><div class="card-body p-4">
      <h2 class="h6 mb-3">This cannot be undone</h2>
      <p class="small text-muted-2">
        There is no route that reverses it and no copy held back. If you want your data first,
        <a href="/profile/data">download it</a> before you continue — afterwards there will be
        nothing to download.
      </p>

      <form method="post" action="/profile/close" class="mt-3">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
        <label class="form-label" for="confirm">Type <strong>ERASE</strong> to confirm</label>
        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <input class="form-control" id="confirm" name="confirm" autocomplete="off"
                 spellcheck="false" style="max-width: 200px" required>
          <button class="btn btn-danger" type="submit">Erase my account</button>
          <a class="btn btn-link" href="/profile/settings">Cancel</a>
        </div>
        <div class="form-text">
          Typed rather than ticked on purpose: a checkbox beside a red button gets clicked by
          habit, and this is the one action nobody can hand back to you.
        </div>
      </form>
    </div></div>
  </div></div>
</div></section>
<%- include('../partials/layout-end') %>
